@title Review: scaling ingredient quantities
@subtitle Notes on scale_ingredient, tied to the lines of the new file

The direction is good. Scaling by a factor, guarding against a zero or negative base, and treating eggs as whole items are all the right ideas. The notes below are about making each of them actually run. One blocks the merge.

kpi Blocker | 1 | line 23 | bad
kpi Major | 2 | lines 27-28, 29 | bad
kpi Minor | 1 | line 30 | neutral

## The change
Line numbers are from the new version of the file.

```python
22  def scale_ingredient(item, servings_from, servings_to):
23 +    if servings_from <= 0:
24 +        raise ValueError("servings_from must be positive")
25      factor = servings_to / servings_from
26      qty = item.qty * factor
27 +    if item.unit in ("tsp", "tbsp") and factor > 3:
28 +        qty = qty * 0.85  # seasoning doesn't scale linearly
29 +    if item.unit == "egg":
30 +        qty = max(1, round(qty))
31      return Ingredient(item.name, round(qty, 1), item.unit)
```

## Notes, in line order

!!! Line 23, blocker: the form posts servings as a string, so this comparison throws on the input from bug #311. Convert to a number before it gets here, or at the form boundary, and then check the result is positive.

!! Lines 27-28, major: 0.85 is a magic number. Priya, our test cook, says it is right for salt only, not for cinnamon or chilli. Give the number a name and decide per ingredient, not per unit.

!! Line 29, major: 1,204 of our 3,010 recipes (40%) store the unit as "eggs", so this condition never matches for them and the rounding silently never runs. Match the unit the data really uses.

! Line 30, minor: halving a 1-egg recipe gives 1 egg, which is wrong. Please add a test that pins down what the result should be.

## Working through them
Do them in this order: the blocker first, then the majors, then the minor.

- [ ] Line 23 (blocker): handle the string input from bug #311
- [ ] Line 29 (major): make the egg check match "eggs"
- [ ] Lines 27-28 (major): name the 0.85 and stop applying it to cinnamon and chilli
- [ ] Line 30 (minor): add a test for halving a 1-egg recipe
